course: dictionary
lesson: 13739
title: Words that show purpose
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you why something happened. Intentionally is one of them. It means on purpose: the person meant to do it, and it was not an accident. «She intentionally left the door open so the cat could get in.» The word tells you the girl planned it.
explain: Look at the words around it to check. «He tripped me up, but it was an accident.» The author says accident, so the tripping was not intentional. Ask yourself: did the person want this to happen? If yes, intentionally fits.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «I did not break the vase intentionally; it slipped from my hands.» Swap in on purpose: «I did not break the vase on purpose; it slipped from my hands» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Intentionally means on purpose.
fact: Intentionally is an adverb, so it tells you how something was done.
fact: «Intentional» is the adjective form, as in «an intentional mistake».
fact: «Accidentally» is the opposite idea: it means by chance, not meaning to.
fact: In school and in law, harm done intentionally is often judged more seriously than harm done by accident.
exercise: «The boy kicked the ball intentionally at the window.» What does intentionally mean? | Very quickly | By accident | Without anyone seeing | *On purpose
exercise: «I did not break the cup intentionally.» Did the person mean to break it? | They broke it twice | Yes, they broke it on purpose | *No, it was an accident | Yes, they planned it
exercise: Which word means nearly the opposite of intentionally? | Proudly | Carefully | *Accidentally | Loudly
test: «She smiled intentionally to make her friend laugh.» What does intentionally show? | She smiled by accident | She forgot her friend | *She meant to make her friend laugh | She was sleeping
test: Which sentence shows an accident? | I tripped on purpose to win a laugh | I planned to spill the juice | *I tripped over my shoelace and nearly fell | I chose to leave the gate open
exam: «He hid the note intentionally so his sister would find it.» What does intentionally tell you? | He dropped it by mistake | He was asleep when it happened | He never wrote the note | *He planned it so she would find it
